Modifications made for this work, as required by Apache License 2.0 Section 4(b),
are described in the README under "Patches to the training and inference stack":

  - vlash/policies/pi05/modeling_pi05.py: exclude keys ending in "_mask" from
    config.input_features so that normalization does not rescale the 0/1 camera
    validity flags.
  - vlash/policies/pi05/modeling_pi05.py: in prepare_images, read
    observation.images.{slot}_mask from the batch per sample and use it as the
    image attention mask, falling back to all-ones when the column is absent.
  - vlash/policies/pi05/modeling_pi05.py: read the PaliGemma tokenizer path from
    the VLASH_PALIGEMMA_PATH environment variable instead of hardcoding the Hub
    id "google/paligemma-3b-pt-224". The Hub id remains the default.
  - vlash/train.py: apply a 224 resize-with-pad image transform when the dataset
    carries "_mask" columns, so that source datasets of mixed resolution can be
    collated.
  - vlash/train.py: on the LoRA branch, save the adapters only, skipping the
    merged model weights and the training state, and export the normalization
    buffers to normalize_buffers.pt.
  - vlash/train.py: upload a rolling resume checkpoint and a permanent archive
    checkpoint to S3 and prune the local copies, driven by the SLOT_ID,
    S3_CKPT_BASE and RESUME_FREQ environment variables. Inactive when unset.
  - vlash/train.py: pin the W&B run id and job name to the slot id and force
    resume="allow" when an S3 slot is configured, so a restarted preemptible
    instance appends to the same run.
  - vlash/run.py: in validate_robot_cameras, accept a subset of the policy's
    camera slots instead of requiring an exact match, while still rejecting
    camera keys the policy does not know.
  - vlash/run.py: add a dry-run mode that computes actions without commanding
    the motors, and an abort when a commanded action exceeds a magnitude bound.
  - vlash/run.py: on a chunk switch, linearly blend the first overlap_steps
    actions of the new action chunk into the last action of the outgoing chunk.
  - vlash/run.py: in load_and_compile_policy, load adapter-only checkpoints
    (base weights plus a LoRA merge) and restore the dataset statistics from
    normalize_buffers.pt.
  - lerobot/datasets/video_utils.py: bound the video decoder cache as an LRU of
    VLASH_DECODER_CACHE_MAX entries and close the file handle on eviction, to
    stop unbounded memory growth over large multi-source datasets.
  - lerobot/datasets/video_utils.py: in decode_video_frames_torchcodec, log the
    offending video path and fall back to frame 0 on a decoder error instead of
    aborting the run.

The four vlash/run.py changes and the tokenizer path change are inference-side.
The camera-subset change is required to run these weights with fewer than three
cameras: upstream validate_robot_cameras compares the robot's camera keys against
the three slots read from the checkpoint and requires an exact match, and it does
so before empty_cameras is applied. The other inference-side changes are
optional. The training-side changes are not required for inference.

